From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:33:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: web notification clicks bring their tab
 forward

Plan C24. Chrome's Mac notification bridge already shows web notifications
in Notification Center for the embedder (banners from the app's own bundle
id, requireInteraction alerts from "Open Arc Helper (Alerts).app"; checked
in usernoted's log). A click now:

- activates the app and reports -tabDidRequestActivation: for the tab of
  the document that showed the notification (the shell selects the tab and
  brings its window forward, as for window.focus());
- when that page is gone, asks OACApplicationDelegate for a foreground tab
  on the notification's origin (application:didRequestNewTab:, opener nil),
  in the profile that showed it.

Uses the //chrome hook of the previous patch, installed when the engine
starts.
---
 openarc/BUILD.gn                            |  3 +
 openarc/bridge/oac_application.mm           |  3 +
 openarc/bridge/oac_notifications.mm         | 87 +++++++++++++++++++++
 openarc/bridge/oac_notifications_internal.h | 18 +++++
 4 files changed, 111 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 openarc/bridge/oac_notifications.mm
 create mode 100644 openarc/bridge/oac_notifications_internal.h

